course: dictionary
lesson: 3133
title: The eleventh one
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Eleventh is a number word that tells you a place in an order. Count the children in a line: first, second, third, and so on, up to the eleventh. Ten come before it, so eleventh is one more than tenth.
explain: The word works in another way too. An eleventh is one of eleven equal parts, written 1/11. If a cake is cut into eleven equal slices, each slice is one eleventh of the cake.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Lessons lasted ten hours the first day, nine the next, and so on.» Alice works out that the eleventh day must have been a holiday, because the lessons count down to nothing. In «at the eleventh hour», the phrase means at the very last moment, so do not look for a clock.
fact: Eleventh means number 11 in order, like the eleventh floor or the eleventh birthday.
fact: An eleventh is one of eleven equal parts, written 1/11.
fact: «At the eleventh hour» means at the very last moment, just in time.
fact: Check the clues: if the sentence is about order, eleventh is a place; if it is about sharing into parts, eleventh is a fraction.
fact: The number 11 is written as «11» and the word is «eleven»; eleventh is the word for its place in order.
exercise: «Lessons lasted ten hours the first day, nine the next.» Alice says the eleventh day must have been a holiday. What does eleventh mean here? | *The eleventh day in order | The last hour before lunch | The first day of the week | An eleven-piece cake
exercise: A cake is cut into eleven equal pieces. What is one piece? | One tenth | Eleven whole cakes | *One eleventh | One half
exercise: Which phrase means at the very last moment? | *At the eleventh hour | At the first hour | At the start of the day | At the bottom of the stairs
test: In a race, Maya finishes in eleventh place. How many runners finished ahead of her? | Eleven | Nine | Twelve | *Ten
test: Which fraction is one of eleven equal parts? | *1/11 | 1/10 | 11/1 | 1/2
exam: Which word means a place in order, as in the eleventh floor? | *eleventh | elevenths | elevens | eleven
